---
// Component: ConversationContinuity
// Demonstrates multi-member and multi-model conversation continuity
---

<div class="conversation-continuity-card" aria-label="Conversation continuity demonstrating switching models seamlessly in one shared chat">
  <div class="conversation-card-header">
    <div class="conversation-topic">
      <span class="topic-tag">Workstream</span>
      <strong>Product strategy & competitive analysis</strong>
    </div>
    <div class="model-switch-badge">
      <span class="switch-icon">⇄</span>
      <span>Continuous Context across 3 AI Models</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="timeline-chat">
    <!-- Turn 1: Team question -->
    <div class="chat-row chat-row--user">
      <div class="chat-author">
        <span class="avatar avatar--vitalii avatar--small">V</span>
        <strong>Vitalii</strong>
      </div>
      <div class="chat-bubble-body">
        <p>Can you draft a value proposition for our new shared AI workspace targeting small agencies?</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Turn 2: Claude response -->
    <div class="chat-row chat-row--ai">
      <div class="chat-author">
        <span class="ai-tag ai-tag--claude">✦ Claude</span>
        <span class="turn-note">via Alex's Worker</span>
      </div>
      <div class="chat-bubble-body">
        <p><strong>Core Value:</strong> "One shared workspace where clients and team members collaborate with best-in-class AI models without sharing sensitive API keys." Emphasize shared context, role-based workflows, and client privacy.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Turn 3: Julia switches model to ChatGPT to critique -->
    <div class="chat-row chat-row--user">
      <div class="chat-author">
        <span class="avatar avatar--julia avatar--small">J</span>
        <strong>Julia</strong>
      </div>
      <div class="chat-bubble-body">
        <p>Let's have <strong>ChatGPT</strong> critique Claude's draft and suggest 3 high-converting hero headlines.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Turn 4: ChatGPT response with inherited context -->
    <div class="chat-row chat-row--ai">
      <div class="chat-author">
        <span class="ai-tag ai-tag--chatgpt">◉ ChatGPT</span>
        <span class="turn-note">inheriting Claude's turn & context</span>
      </div>
      <div class="chat-bubble-body">
        <p>Building directly on Claude's positioning for agencies:</p>
        <ol class="chat-list">
          <li><strong>"Stop screenshotting ChatGPT. Bring your agency and AI together."</strong> (Direct pain point)</li>
          <li><strong>"The shared AI workspace for creative and technical teams."</strong> (Clear category)</li>
          <li><strong>"Collaborate with your clients, your team, and your AI — in one place."</strong> (Collaboration focus)</li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="conversation-card-footer">
    <div class="footer-feature">
      <span class="feature-bullet">✓</span>
      <span><strong>Zero context loss:</strong> Every model sees prior discussion, attachments, and decisions.</span>
    </div>
    <div class="footer-feature">
      <span class="feature-bullet">✓</span>
      <span><strong>No copy-pasting:</strong> No more shuttling prompts between separate browser tabs.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
